[Music]  are you ready for the uk  transition number four resources  and support  hello my name is jane rose and i'm head  of international trade at the essex  chambers of commerce  this is the last of four bite-sized  videos about the uk transition  which have been commissioned by rochford  district council to help businesses  prepare  for the changes to trading with the eu  in this final video  i want to look at what resources are out  there and where you can find information  and training to help you prepare for the  uk transition  contact and website details are listed  in the video description  a good place to start is our essex  chambers uk transition website page  we've selected core information to help  you find what you need  quickly and we're updating the site all  of the time  we're running lots of online training  courses that can help you with all  aspects of importing and exporting  but i can't stress enough that you need  to learn about customers processes  especially if you've never traded  outside of the eu  but there is government funding  available for training staff  and it software if you're thinking of  making your own customs declarations  it might be useful to connect to the  government agencies that provide  guidance for specific sectors like food  and drink for example  and you should find out what  certificates licenses or other  arrangements might be needed  you should also look at packaging and  labeling requirements for your products  are there changes how will you label  your products and what type of pallets  can be used  you should also review any contracts you  have in place  if you use inco terms which set out the  responsibility between the buyer and the  seller  you'll need to check how the transition  affects those responsibilities  find out if you're going to need to  produce export documentation  like certificates of origin or customs  documents  essex chambers can help you with this  you'll also need to make sure that you  know the origin of your goods  where they originate from not just where  they're imported from  and you'll need proof of origin you'll  need to refer to the uk global tariff  and the exporters trade tool to see what  commodity codes and duties will be for  your products  and you should be aware of changes that  will impact the transportation of your  goods speak with your transport and  logistics providers  if you're importing and exporting to  northern ireland you need to sign up to  the traders  support service this will guide you  through any changes due to the  implementation of the northern ireland  protocol  is not just physical goods that are  affected if you're providing services in  the eu  you need to check the national  regulations on the government selling  services guide  i would advise looking at the border  operating model it is a huge document  and it won't all apply to you but  everything you need to know  is in there finally sign up for the  government updates and alerts  and stay informed there's a lot to think  about and not a lot of time to prepare  if you haven't already  on behalf of essex chambers and rochford  district council  we hope the videos have been of help to  you and please do contact us if you need  help  my final advice would be to find out  where the responsibilities lie for you  as a business all of the links to the  topics i've spoken about  and the government guidance can be found  in the video descriptions together with  contact details  thank you so much for listening  [Music]  you

